@startuml
title Task 2.2 - Sequence Diagram: UC-18 Checkout, stock and idempotent payment
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
actor Customer
participant "Next.js UI" as UI
participant "NestJS API" as API
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Mock Payment Service" as Pay

Customer -> UI: Confirm cart; optional promotion code
opt Customer needs to sign in
  UI -> API: POST /auth/login or /auth/register
  API --> UI: User profile + JWT
end
UI -> API: POST /orders\nBearer JWT, items, promotionCode?
activate API
API -> API: Verify JWT; validate DTO and options
API -> API: Recalculate prices from trusted product data
opt Promotion code entered
  API -> DB: Read promotion and validate conditions
  DB --> API: Valid/invalid result
  API -> API: Calculate final total
end
alt Invalid request or JWT
  API --> UI: 400 validation / 401 unauthorized
  UI --> Customer: Show error; keep cart
else Valid request
  group Transaction 1: create order and reserve inventory
    API -> DB: BEGIN
    API -> DB: Read stock and version
    alt Out of stock or version conflict
      API -> DB: ROLLBACK
      API --> UI: 409 inventory conflict
      UI --> Customer: Show unavailable item; keep cart
    else Stock is sufficient
      API -> DB: INSERT Order(PENDING) and OrderItems
      API -> DB: UPDATE/reserve stock with optimistic version check
      API -> DB: COMMIT
      DB --> API: orderId, item snapshots, total
      API --> UI: 201 Created
      UI --> Customer: Show order and payment options
    end
  end
end

opt Order creation succeeded; customer starts payment
  Customer -> UI: Choose Wallet/Card and confirm
  UI -> API: POST /payments\nBearer JWT, orderId, method\nIdempotency-Key
  API -> DB: Find prior key; verify user/order/state
  alt Same key and same payload
    DB --> API: Stored result
    API --> UI: Return prior outcome; no duplicate work
  else Same key and different payload
    API --> UI: 409 conflict
  else New key
    API -> Pay: Process simulated payment outside DB transaction
    alt Payment SUCCESS
      Pay --> API: SUCCESS
      group Transaction 2: record payment result
        API -> DB: BEGIN
        API -> DB: INSERT Payment; transition Order to PAID
        API -> DB: INSERT LoyaltyTransaction once per order
        API -> DB: COMMIT
      end
      API --> UI: 200 result (PAID, orderId)
      UI --> Customer: Show confirmation
      UI -> UI: Clear cart
    else Payment FAILED
      Pay --> API: FAILED
      group Transaction 2: record payment result
        API -> DB: BEGIN
        API -> DB: INSERT Payment; transition Order to PAYMENT_FAILED
        API -> DB: COMMIT
      end
      API --> UI: 200 failure outcome
      UI --> Customer: Show failure; keep cart
      note over Customer,UI
      Retry confirmed failure with a new key on the same order.
      Replay of the same request reuses its original key.
      end note
    end
  end
end
deactivate API
@enduml
